    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d214-a1">

                <pb facs="0320" n="320" sameAs="frus:frus1861/pg320"/>

                <head>Card.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States
                            Legation</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Turin</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-05-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 17, 1861</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In reply to numerous and continued applications to this legation, by letter and
                    in person, of foreign volunteers for enlistment in the army of the United States
                    of America, the undersigned takes this public means of declaring that he has no
                    knowledge, official or non-official, of any instructions of his government
                    authorizing any such enlistments out of the United States.</p>
                <closer><signed>ROMAINE DILLON,</signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé
                        d’Affaires, &amp;c.</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
